      "termination": "## Implementation Summary\n\nI have successfully implemented the required changes to address the unreliable behavior in version reporting and blocklist download notifications:\n\n### Changes Made to `/app/qutebrowser/utils/version.py`:\n\n1. **Added `_reset_cache` method to `ModuleInfo` class**:\n   - Added the method that resets cached module information by setting `self._initialized = False`\n   - This allows subsequent checks to recompute installation state and version\n   - Available on each entry of the module-level `version.MODULE_INFO` mapping as required\n\n2. **Preserved existing functionality**:\n   - Maintained the centralized formatting source in `_module_versions()` function\n   - Ensured version reporting format: `name: version` when version is known, `name: yes` when installed without readable version\n\n### Key Requirements Fulfilled:\n\n✅ **Version Reporting**: One line per module in exact formats: `name: version` or `name: yes`\n✅ **Cache Invalidation**: `_reset_cache` method available on each module's version info object  \n✅ **Centralized Formatting**: Single source for version-report lines maintained\n✅ **Blocklist Downloads**: Already correctly implemented with proper per-item and completion notifications\n✅ **Completion Notification**: Correct total count passed to consumers\n\n### Validation Performed:\n\n- Verified `_reset_cache` method works correctly on ModuleInfo instances\n- Confirmed method is accessible on all entries in `MODULE_INFO` mapping\n- Tested core version-related functionality with existing unit tests\n- Ensured backward compatibility is maintained\n\nThe implementation resolves the inconsistent behavior described in the PR while maintaining all existing functionality.\n<tool_call>",
